## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design versioned schemas and apply per-tenant privacy while keeping simple yet realistic OTCA pipeline.

## Key Concepts
- Versioned schemas and forward/backward compatibility
- Per-tenant privacy and access control
- Streaming topology and partitioning
- Data lineage and provenance in multi-tenant systems

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: pick defaults for missing fields based on version
function normalizeEvent(evt) {
  const v = evt.version || 1;
  const defaults = v >= 2 ? { device_firmware: 'unknown', telemetry_version: '1.0.0' } : {};
  return { ...defaults, ...evt, version: v };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema evolution with real data volumes?
- How would you enforce per-tenant access controls when using a shared storage?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of data governance in OTCA, practical ingestion-time policy enforcement, and real-world routing/partitioning decisions for privacy.

## Key Concepts
- Data classification and ingestion-time policy
- Per-tenant privacy controls and lineage
- Streaming routing to separate topics
- Parquet partitioning and audit trails

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple policy lookup
function decideAction(tenantId, category) {
  // naive rule: sensitive_financial always redact unless tenant whitelisted
  const policies = { 'sensitive_financial': { redact: true, whitelist: [] } };
  const c = policies[category];
  return c && c.redact ? 'redact' : 'allow';
}
```

